From: Menno van Leeuwen <menno@vleeuwen.me>
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: qca: configure preinitialized Myron without reset

The Xiaomi Myron WCN786x is initialized by a userspace loader before the
QCA line discipline is attached.  Repeated HCI commands work after that
handoff, but HCI Reset leaves the controller accepting IBS wake handshakes
without returning later HCI command responses.  Both BlueZ discovery and a
raw UART reproducer hit this boundary.

Set HCI_QUIRK_RESET_ON_CLOSE before hci_register_dev() only for the
explicit non-serdev qca_preinitialized path.  Mark that controller as
requiring a public address and expose QCA's set_bdaddr callback from the
preinitialized setup path.  The Bluetooth management API can then program
the address from the already downloaded, hash-pinned NVM without issuing
the HCI Reset that wedges this controller.  Every default QCA path is
unchanged.

This remains an experimental one-shot path.  Reset-on-close may leave this
controller unusable until the existing btpower cleanup power-cycles it.
---
 drivers/bluetooth/hci_qca.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_qca.c b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_qca.c
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_qca.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_qca.c
@@ -599,6 +599,17 @@ static int qca_open(struct hci_uart *hu)
 	qca->vote_last_jif = jiffies;
 
 	hu->priv = qca;
+	if (!hu->serdev && READ_ONCE(qca_preinitialized)) {
+		/* The Myron userspace handoff has already initialized the
+		 * controller. HCI Reset makes that firmware stop answering
+		 * later commands, so defer Reset until this one-shot transport
+		 * closes and the guarded cleanup power-cycles the controller.
+		 */
+		set_bit(HCI_QUIRK_RESET_ON_CLOSE, &hu->hdev->quirks);
+		set_bit(HCI_QUIRK_USE_BDADDR_PROPERTY, &hu->hdev->quirks);
+		bt_dev_info(hu->hdev,
+			    "preinitialized controller; skipping opening HCI Reset");
+	}
 
 	if (hu->serdev) {
 		qcadev = serdev_device_get_drvdata(hu->serdev);
@@ -1874,6 +1885,7 @@ static int qca_setup(struct hci_uart *hu)
 		qca->tty_pm = true;
 		clear_bit(QCA_IBS_DISABLED, &qca->flags);
 		set_bit(HCI_QUIRK_SIMULTANEOUS_DISCOVERY, &hdev->quirks);
+		hdev->set_bdaddr = qca_set_bdaddr;
 		qca_debugfs_init(hdev);
 
 		return 0;
-- 
